# AI & Socket.IO (Backend)

## Anthropic – `generateAIContent`

```js
import { generateAIContent } from "../config/aiModal.js";

const text = await generateAIContent(promptString, maxTokens);
// Returns: string (first content block text from Claude)
```

Model and API key come from `process.env.ANTHROPIC_MODEL_NAME` / `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (via `constant/index.js`).

### Token Budgets

| Feature | Max Tokens |
|---|---|
| AI comment (`suggest-comment/:id`) | 100 |
| AI post draft (`suggest-posts`) | 300 |
| Chatbot response | 250 |

Keep prompts short and instructional. Avoid large context payloads.

## Chatbot – `processChatMessage`

Located in `controllers/chatbot.controllers.js`. Called by the socket handler:

```js
// config/socket.js
socket.on("chat-message", async ({ message, intent }) => {
  const reply = await processChatMessage(socket.userId, message, intent);
  socket.emit("bot-reply", { content: reply });
});
```

### Intent Classification (no LLM cost)

`classifyIntent(text)` uses regex – runs before any AI call:

| Intent | Trigger keywords |
|---|---|
| `post_idea` | "post idea", "what to post", "suggest post", "content idea" |
| `top_topics` | "trending", "top topic", "hot topic", "popular" |
| `profile_stats` | "follower", "stats", "engagement", "my profile", "analytics" |
| `latest_post` | "latest post", "last post", "recent post", "my last" |
| `search` | "search", "find", "looking for" |
| `general` | (default) |

Response is truncated to 250 characters before returning to the client.

## Socket.IO Setup

```js
// config/socket.js
export const userSocketMap = new Map(); // userId (string) → socketId (string)
export function setupSocket(server) { ... }

// index.js
export const io = setupSocket(server);
```

Socket auth middleware verifies JWT from `socket.handshake.auth.token` and sets `socket.userId`.

Register users on connect:
```js
socket.on("register", (userId) => {
  userSocketMap.set(userId, socket.id);
});
```

## Content Moderation Middleware

`middlewares/aiModeration.js` – checks `req.body.description | content | aiPrompt`:

1. **Profanity/spam** – `bad-words` Filter + custom `spamWordsList` (from `constant/index.js`)
2. **Regex pattern** – tests against escaped `spamWordsList`
3. **Duplicate detection** – `string-similarity.compareTwoStrings` threshold `> 0.9` against all existing posts

Returns `400 { success: false, message }` on failure; calls `next()` if clean.

> Currently commented out in `post.routes.js`. To re-enable:
> ```js
> import { aiModeration } from "../middlewares/aiModeration.js";
> postRoutes.post("/create-post", isAuth, upload.single("image"), aiModeration, createPost);
> postRoutes.post("/comment/:id", isAuth, aiModeration, commentOnPost);
> ```
